so  democratic senator  uh uh ostensibly democratic senator joe  manchin yesterday  gave a press conference on this spending  and infrastructure bill that he has been  uh an obstacle to actually getting  passed gave a press conference yesterday  that i can only describe to you as  kafkaesque now what what does  kafka-esque mean  fans of the tv series breaking bad might  recognize the word kafka-esque i've used  it a few times before it's really the  only word i can think of to describe  this and you'll see why in a second  kafka-esque means having a nightmarishly  complex  bizarre or illogical quality  of the example that merriam-webster  gives is that sometimes there are  kafka-esque bureaucratic delays  um  my birth country of argentina  i think is arguably best known for  kafka-esque bureaucracy problems but  that's a story for a different day i'm  gonna play some clips for you from this  joe manchin  uh press conference  in this clip i mean everything is just  backwards  joe manchin says hey listen  he's been working on this bill for three  months  and  he's urging the house to vote and pass  the bipartisan infrastructure bill take  a listen to this i've worked in good  faith for three months for the past  three months with president biden leader  schumer speaker pelosi and my colleagues  on the reconciliation bill  and i will continue to do so  for the sake of the country i urge the  house to vote and pass the bipartisan  infrastructure bill  joe you've been one of the primary  holdups in actually getting to a bill  that  everybody will be happy with in terms of  democrats in the senate and he now is  framing this as the fact that the house  won't vote and pass the bill he wants to  be law  means  he is no longer part of the problem  think about the backwards framing his  framing is listen when joe biden wants  to talk to me i talk to him i negotiate  with democrats i negotiate with  republicans and yet the house won't vote  on the bipartisan infrastructure bill  ignoring the fact that there's multiple  components here and multiple bills  that there is a desire to pass these in  tandem and that he has been like a  stubborn little kid that nobody can  placate who just wants attention and is  clearly enjoying the attention but he's  saying it's everybody else's fault not  mine  next clip  here he says he won't support any bill  unless he has clarity as to the impact  on inflation of that bill i for one  won't support a multi-trillion dollar  bill without greater clarity about why  congress chooses to ignore the serious  effects of inflation  and debt that have on our economy and  existing government programs these are  just the same old tired talking points  we know  uh the effect of government programs and  of government spending has he sought  clarity on it  has he spoken to economic experts about  this because these answers are available  these are not things to which we can't  find clarity and now  throwing in the typically republican  political football of our the debt the  debt the debt our debt  and then in completely you know  it's just  i don't even know what to call it  fashion  joe manchin says hey let's quit playing  games and pass the bill yeah joe you're  the one playing the games  it's time to pass the bill and quit  playing games  irony is dead  irony is dead joe manchin says let's  stop the games and pass the bill  now does he recognize the absurdity of  what he's saying and the fact that he's  the reason that  not the only reason one of the main  reasons  that we haven't yet seen a bill passed  is he the one playing games or is he  really so naive that he sees everybody  else as creating problems rather than  him  irony is dead and this is again another  reminder  uh in west virginia  you either get this or you get a  full-blown republican so the solution  isn't  to primary joe manchin  from an emotional standpoint maybe it is  maybe a lot of people would feel good  primarying joe manchin if somehow  uh uh someone to his left wins the  primary  then they lose the general  and that seat gets flipped from democrat  to republican okay maybe some people  would feel good about that because they  would feel like he lost his seat it's a  punishment to him  as we talked about with bill share and  uh and and with members of the audience  over the last couple of weeks  the real solution is you got to flip  republican seats to democrats i continue  to maintain that's the solution if you  disagree with me let me know  one of our sponsors is curiosity stream  the only subscription streaming service  dedicated to documentaries if you're  like me you're always watching  documentaries you want to find the best  ones and curiosity stream is really a  must-have curiosity stream has a better  selection of documentaries than netflix  hulu or amazon i just finished watching  wasteland about  a landfill  on the outskirts of rio in brazil  where  men and women sift through garbage  in order to try to make some money it's  horrifying but extraordinarily well done  they always have the newest and most  critically acclaimed titles when you're  looking for good documentaries use the  streaming service that specializes in  documentaries that's why i use  curiositystream they have documentaries  on politics economics history technology  psychology  everything if you love documentaries  you've got to have curiosity stream you  will see what i mean when you start  using it when you go to curiositystream  curiositystream.com pacman you'll get 25  off a subscription which comes out to  just 15 bucks a year the link is right  underneath this video

